---
# What CI fails on, along with cppcheck. Each check turned off here has its reason:
#
# performance-enum-size: saving a few bytes on enums isn't worth it here.
# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: most functions with two strings or two ints would need changing.
# bugprone-narrowing-conversions: mostly UI coordinates and sizes between int, float and lv_coord_t.
# bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result: mostly constants, like 7 * 24 * 3600, and none overflow.
# performance-inefficient-string-concatenation: these aren't in hot paths, and + reads better.
# bugprone-branch-clone: separate branches with the same body often read better, as in a switch on type.
# bugprone-reserved-identifier: comes from forward declaring LVGL's own types, like _lv_group_t.
# bugprone-suspicious-enum-usage: LVGL combines part and state flags from different enums by design.
# performance-no-int-to-ptr: LVGL passes small integers as user data pointers by design.
# clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.strcpy: only flags copies into buffers just sized from the same string.
# clang-analyzer-optin.cplusplus.VirtualCall: destructors calling their own shutdown(), which is what's meant.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -performance-inefficient-string-concatenation,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-branch-clone,
  -bugprone-reserved-identifier,
  -bugprone-suspicious-enum-usage,
  -performance-no-int-to-ptr,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.strcpy,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.cplusplus.VirtualCall
HeaderFilterRegex: '(app/include|shared/include|app/src)/.*'
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
...
